 "title": "UPI: Muft app se roz Rs 1 lakh crore tak ka safar | Case Study #shorts",
 "description": "Roz 82 crore UPI payment aur roz ka average Rs 1 lakh crore+! Ek muft app ne ye kaise kiya? Case study.\n\n- 25 Aug 2016 launch: pehle saal ~1.78 crore transaction, 44 bank\n- 3 chaalein: user ke liye muft, koi bhi app-koi bhi bank, har thele par QR\n- FY26: 24,162 crore+ transaction (~13,000 guna), 703 bank\n- Oct 2026: 25.47 arab transaction, record\n- Twist: Rs 2,000+ ke kuch merchant payments par 0.4% MDR (max Rs 300) ka plan, abhi Diwali ke baad tak tala\n\nSources:\nhttps://india.entrepreneur.com/business-news/upi-hits-record-25-47-bn-transactions-in-october-daily-value-crosses-inr-1-l-cr\nhttps://telanganatoday.com/upi-transactions-surge-13000-fold-to-24162-crore-in-fy26\nhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/business/upi-transactions-fall-18-in-september-to-2407-billion-ahead-of-october-15-mdr-rollout\n\nPhotos (Wikimedia Commons):\nFile:Street vendor's mobile stall in India.jpg | Nalbarian | CC BY-SA 4.0\nFile:India - Varanasi green peas - 2714.jpg | Jorge Royan | CC BY-SA 3.0\nFile:India - Varanasi paper bag maker - 0078.jpg | Jorge Royan | CC BY-SA 3.0\nFile:Chai walli - Old woman at a Tea Stall on a highway in Pauri, Uttrakhand, India.jpg | Photopayal | CC BY-SA 4.0\nFile:India - Varanasi chai tea - 1420.jpg | Jorge Royan | CC BY-SA 3.0\nFile:Chai (Tea) Stall.jpg | Vidurmayor | CC BY-SA 4.0\nFile:Bank of India, Mumbai main branch as viewed from right side.jpg | DesiBoy101 | CC BY-SA 4.0\nFile:Bank of India, Mumbai main branch as viewed from left side.jpg | DesiBoy101 | CC BY-SA 4.0\n\n#shorts #casestudy #upi #digitalindia #60seckhabar",
